<NPCCharacters>
  <!-- Fully independent Crusader States (Culture.vlandia) troop tree - new character ids, own
       upgrade chain, own equipment loadouts, mirroring byzantine_custom_troops.xml/
       abbasid_custom_troops.xml/georgian_custom_troops.xml exactly. Does NOT reuse or touch
       Native's vlandia_recruit/vlandia_militia/etc troops. Every equipment item id below is a
       real, already-shipped Native item (verified against SandBoxCore/ModuleData/items/*.xml's
       own <Item>/<CraftedItem> definitions).
       Tier structure (6/11/16/21/26/31) and per-tier skill-point totals (90/195/360/508/676/835)
       match this mod's own audited standard, reusing byzantine_custom_troops.xml's exact
       per-branch skill numbers since the branch roles line up directly (infantry/ranged/light
       cavalry/heavy cavalry) - only the ranged branch's skill type changes (Crossbow instead of
       Bow, since the crossbow was the Franks' actual signature ranged weapon, not reflavored).
       Historical grounding: Sergeants (both foot and mounted, saw far more combat use than
       knights per capita and were core Crusader men-at-arms), Turcopoles (locally-recruited
       mounted archers, up to half of a Crusader army's cavalry by the mid-12th century),
       Knights and the "Knight banneret" rank (a knight entitled to lead troops under his own
       square banner), and the Hospitaller and Templar military-religious orders (founded 1099
       and 1119 respectively - both founded within this mod's own timeframe) as the elite endpoint
       of the infantry and heavy cavalry lines. -->

